<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/3/23/text/60>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 60 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/3/23> ;
      zoo:text "A. 492 A 14 Ἀλκμαίων οὐκ ἀληθῆ λέγει, φάμενος ἀναπνεῖν τὰς αἶγας κατὰ τὰ ὦτα [quoted G. White, N. H. of Selborne, Letter XIV ]; Plin. VIII .202 auribus eas spirare, non naribus, . . . Archelaus auctor est . Cf. Ael. I .53; Varro II .3.5. ❦" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/1/text/51>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 51 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/1> ;
      zoo:text "in his mother's womb. O whata heart, what a mind have mortal men! They do as they list; they make horses of varied colours while yet enveloped in the milky mother's loins. What time the mating impulse seizes the mare and she abides the approach of the glorious high-spirited horse, then they cunningly adorn the beautiful sire. All about they inscribe all his body with spots of colour and to his bride they lead him, glorying in his beauty. Even as some youth, arrayed by the bridal women in white robes and purple flowers and breathing of the perfume of Palestine,steps into the bridal chamber singing the marriage song, so while the hasting horse neighs his bridal song, long time in front of his bride they stay her glorious spouse, foaming in his eagerness; and late and at last they let him go to satisfy his desire. And the mare conceives and bears a many-patterned foal, having received in her womb the fertile seed of her spouse, but in her eyes his many-coloured form." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2/text/104>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 104 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "ἄδην· αὐταρκῶς, δαψιλῶς (schol.); cf. Hesych. ἄδην· ἀθρόως, ἐξαίφνης, δαψιλῶς. ἀλιοντ’ αὐδήν K, Boudreaux, perhaps rightly. Dual for plural is common in late epic." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2/text/116>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 116 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "Steph. Byz." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2/text/128>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 128 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "Paus. VIII.43.3; Ridg. pp242 and 248." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2/text/249>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 249 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "Oppian seems to denote by this name two species of horses: (1) with neck and back striped like tiger, (2) spotted like leopard. The first he regards as a natural breed, the second as an artificial production. Cf. τοὺς μὲν πρώτους ἡ φύσις οὕτω διεζωγράφησε, τῶν δευτέρων δ’ ἀνδρῶν εὑρήματα τὰ ποικίλματα. The first suggests the zebra." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2/text/129>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 129 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "Arr. C. 1.4, 23.2;" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2/text/237>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 237 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "Thayer's Note: Also Aetna, 71-73." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2/text/358>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 358 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "Poll. V.65. But Arr. C. 6 τὰ δὲ χρώματα οὐδὲν διοίσει ὁποῖα ἂν ἔχωσιν, οὐδ’ εἰ παντελῶς εἶεν μέλαιναι ἢ πυρραὶ ἢ λευκαί· οὐδὲ τὸ ἁπλοῦν χρὴ ὑποπτεύειν τῆς χρόας ὡς θηριῶδες." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2/text/346>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 346 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "Xen. l.c. στήθη πλατέα μὴ ἄσαρκα. Cf. Poll. l.c.; Arr. C. 5.9; Colum. l.c. amplo vilosoque pectore." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/OPPIANUS-2/cynegetica/e/2/text/225>
